      <body>
         <head>Jacky Dandy's Delight</head>
         <author>Jacky Dandy</author>
         <p rend="color(#000000)">{{GUTENBERG_LICENSE}}</p>
         <p rend="start color(#000000)">en-gutenberg-odts/j/Jacky Dandys Delight.23482.odt</p>
         <p>Transcriber’s Note: Spelling and inconsistent formatting of poems has been maintained as in the original.</p>
         <head>Jacky Dandy’s<lb/>DELIGHT.</head>
         <p>image</p>
         <p>This is Mr. Harliquin, who<lb/>shews what is to be seen<lb/>within.</p>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>Jacky Dandy's Delight</head>
            <pb/>
            <div type="div2">
               <head>LONDON:</head>
               <lg>
                  <l>Printed and Sold by J. Pitts,</l>
                  <l>6, Great St. Andrew</l>
                  <l>Street, 7 Dial</l>
               </lg>
            </div>
         </div>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>JACKY DANDY.</head>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is little Jacky Dandy</l>
               <l>  He loves cake and sugar-candy,</l>
               <l>  He bought some at the grocer’s shop,</l>
               <l>  And pleased away went hop, hop, hop.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">He hopp’d to the fair,<lb/>And saw a show there.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The first was the Lion,</l>
               <l>  That never would yield;</l>
               <l>  Behold how he ranger,</l>
               <l>  The King of the field.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">He next saw the Wolf, a cruel and savage beast.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is the Wolf,</l>
               <l>  That prouls thro’ the wood,</l>
               <l>  Who preys upon lambs,</l>
               <l>  And drinks of their blood.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">He was next shewn a Monkey, a funny fellow, but mischievous.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The monkey mischievous</l>
               <l>  Like a naughty boy looks,</l>
               <l>  Who plagues all his friends,</l>
               <l>  And don’t mind his books.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was a Bear, that had been taught to dance.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is the Bear,</l>
               <l>  In Greenland was bred,</l>
               <l>  And brought over here,</l>
               <l>  Thro’ the streets to be led.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was the Tiger.</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The savage Tiger will, they say,</l>
               <l>  Sieze any man that’s in his way,</l>
               <l>  And o’er his back the victim throw,</l>
               <l>  As you your satchel may do now.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">He now saw a little Robin Red-breast hopping about.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>He cocks his tail,</l>
               <l>  While hopping along,</l>
               <l>  And pays for his crumbs</l>
               <l>  With an innocent song.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was little Jenny Wren the smallest bird in England.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The little Robin</l>
               <l>  And the Wren,</l>
               <l>  Are Jacky Dandy’s</l>
               <l>  Cock and Hren.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was a Kite a cruel enemy to all small birds.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is the Kite,</l>
               <l>  When searching for food</l>
               <l>  Kills Bob and his wife,</l>
               <l>  And all the young brood.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was a Goose, some say a silly bird but good roasted.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is the Goose,</l>
               <l>  That wadles and swims,</l>
               <l>  See, little boy,</l>
               <l>  How foolish she seems.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was a beautiful Game Cock with fine comb and gills.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is the Cock</l>
               <l>  Who crows, if you’re wise,</l>
               <l>  To tell you from bed</l>
               <l>  ’Tis time for to rise.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was a Hen and Chickens—See, there is one on her Back.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is the Hen</l>
               <l>  Who cares for her young,</l>
               <l>  And cackles to please them</l>
               <l>  Instead of a song.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was a very fine Newfoundland Dog.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is the Dog,</l>
               <l>  Who whilst we’re asleep,</l>
               <l>  Is a guard to the house,</l>
               <l>  And from thieves does it keep.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">The next was a nice Cat who sat purring a song.</p>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This is poor Puss,</l>
               <l>  The beautiful Cat,</l>
               <l>  That keeps the house clear,</l>
               <l>  Of both Mouse and Rat.</l>
            </lg>
         </div>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>CONCLUSION.</head>
            <p rend="justify">image</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Now you’ve all the Beast</l>
               <l>  And the Birds that are handy,</l>
               <l>  Take this horse and ride home</l>
               <l>  With little Jack Dandy.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">Pitts Toy Warehouse.</p>
         </div>
      </body>
